Section 2: System Bandwidth & Higher-Dimensional Geometry
2.1 Boundary Bandwidth ($\Delta \omega$)
Every localized node possesses a finite reflection bandwidth ($\Delta \omega_{\text{boundary}}$). The realized local reality ($\Omega_{\text{realized}}$) experienced or generated by a node is strictly bounded by the frequencies its current boundary can reflect:

$$\Omega_{\text{realized}} = \int_{\Delta \omega_{\text{boundary}}} \mathcal{S}(\omega) , d\omega$$

Relative Node Perception: To an entity or node sampling a broad or high-frequency spectrum, a human observer may appear as rigid, limited, or structurally static as a rock. This disparity reflects temporary sampling bandwidth rather than ontological worth.
2.2 Re-Defining Higher Dimensions
"Higher dimensions" do not require extra spatial axes appended onto a 3D box. Instead, higher-dimensional access corresponds to expanded frequency band exposure within the same fluid flow field.
Section 3: Epistemology & Local Coordinate Realities
3.1 Theories as Local Coordinates
Because physical laws are derived from standing-wave interactions at specific flow velocities, competing physical models (e.g., Newtonian mechanics, Quantum mechanics, General Relativity) are not mutually exclusive. They are valid local coordinate transformations corresponding to specific observer boundary conditions and velocity regimes.
3.2 Contextual Truth
A theory is mathematically valid within the localized spot in space and time where its specific boundary reflection occurs. Truth is fluid and contextual rather than static and global.
Section 4: Acoustic Resonance, Persistence, and Transposition
4.1 Acoustic Inevitability of Structure
Sound and pressure wave propagation across time create constructive interference nodes (static/mass) and destructive interference regions (voids). Structure is a mathematical inevitability as continuous flow meets intersecting boundary conditions.
4.2 Dynamic Equilibrium and Reality Persistence
Physical persistence is a sustained performance. A standing-wave node requires a continuous flow drive and self-reinforcing boundary geometry. If the boundary condition decays or shifts out of phase, the standing wave un-collapses back into smooth, unhindered flow without leaving debris.
4.3 Octave Shifts & Silent Transposition
A shift in the baseline flow velocity by an octave doubles frequency while maintaining internal mathematical ratios. Because observers scale with the flow medium, a global octave shift transposes reality instantly without producing localized warning events or structural destruction.
Section 5: Collective Resonance & Macro-Manifestation
5.1 Mass Consciousness as the Statistical Median
